# Session backup artifacts (throwaway)
Nova_backups/
Nova_backup*.zip
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
reference/

# Throwaway debugging/bug-hunt scratch scripts (never part of the program)
scratch-*.js
scratch/
port-experiment-groups.json

# runtime telemetry log (regenerated each run)
logs/telemetry.jsonl

# Test-suite run logs (node run-tests.js > _suiteN.txt) — regenerated on every run.
_suite*.txt

# Internal working notes — kept on disk, never published.
#
# These are the bug-hunt ledgers, session handoffs and planning documents the
# project is developed against. They are not addressed to users: several are
# written to whoever picks the work up next, and several are lists of defects
# that were still open when they were written. Publishing them alongside a
# release invites both confusion and misreading, so they stay local.
#
# Untracked 2026-08-25 before the 1.0.6 release. They remain in git history —
# this only stops them appearing in the repo tree from here on.
AI_SUMMARY.md
AUTOSESSION_NOTES.md
HANDOFF.md
SESSION_HANDOFF.md
DESIGN_TOOLS_PROPOSAL.md
MAP_EDITOR_PLAN.md
REORG_PLAN.md
UPDATER_PROPOSAL.md
HOI4_FEATURE_AUDIT.md
ROADMAP.md
RELEASE-NOTES-v*.md

# Bug-hunt findings + progress ledgers (all _-prefixed working files).
_*.md

# Bug-hunt verdict dumps and tmp catalogues — the JSON siblings of the _*.md
# ledgers above. Same reason: adversarial-verification output and scratch data,
# regenerated on demand, never addressed to a user.
_verdicts.json
_build-defects.json
_build-verdicts.json
*.tmp_catalog.json

# Debug/tooling artifacts — referenced by no code, kept locally, never published.
repomix-output.xml
snaps/
md-research-gui-*.gui

# Built executables — releases are attached to a GitHub release, never committed.
# A 98 MB unsigned exe from 1.0.2 (under the old project name) sat in the repo
# root for months and was ~99% of what a clone downloaded.
*.exe
!Texconv.exe

# The third-party notices are written here by scripts/gen-third-party-notices.js before every build (the prebuild
# hooks), from what actually ships, and build.extraFiles copies them next to the exe. Never typed and never committed:
# a hand-kept copy is exactly what goes stale between releases.
/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt

# Back-out controls: a test patches server.js and requires the copy, so `.ctl-<test>-<pid>.js` is a whole
# ~2 MB server with a deliberate bug in it. Each test removes its own in a finally block, but a crash or a
# Ctrl-C leaves one behind — and a later `git add -A` would commit a broken server beside the real one.
.ctl-*.js
